      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "Imager versions before 1.036 for Perl exit the process reading a TGA with a colour map length of 32768 or more in tga_palette_read.\n\nThe reader unpacks the two-byte colour map length into a signed short, so a length of 32768 or more becomes negative. tga_palette_read() casts that value to size_t and asks mymalloc() for a size near SIZE_MAX. The allocation fails and Imager's allocator calls exit(3).\n\nReading an attacker-supplied file through Imager->read() triggers an uncatchable exit.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
